#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100578 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc8166bb-3a9d-5808-af53-a18ca99920f8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Sine Function"}] :question/id #uuid "48da9a24-92e2-5b0c-a92e-65fa2a81ff4f" :question/math-academy-id "e-3779" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$\\sin{\\left(4x-90^\\circ\\right)} = -\\dfrac{1}{2}$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x - 90^{∘} &= -30^{∘} + 360^{∘}n, \\mid 4x - 90^{∘}|=-150^{∘} + 360^{∘}n\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x$, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}4x &= 90^{∘} - 30^{∘} + 360^{∘}n & 4x|= 90^{∘} - 150^{∘} + 360^{∘}n \\\\ 4x|= 60^{∘} + 360^{∘}n & 4x|=-60^{∘} + 360^{∘}n \\\\ x|= 15^{∘} + 90^{∘}n & x|=-15^{∘} + 90^{∘}n\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100579 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97786302-e865-5581-b08e-8da7c6b7a01b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/id #uuid "857ee3a0-9f63-531c-a06c-285e67846f0b" :question/math-academy-id "e-3780" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation:\n$\\tan\\left(2x - \\dfrac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = -1$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x - \\frac{π}{4} &= -\\frac{π}{4} + nπ\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x &= nπ \\\\\nx &= \\frac{nπ}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100580 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ea83062-5744-52ef-9b3e-f9805ed092fb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Reciprocal Function"}] :question/id #uuid "0d83d1d9-82cc-5d34-a335-1f49fbabd194" :question/math-academy-id "e-3781" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation:\n$\\sec\\left(2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\sqrt{2}$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{4} + 2\\pi n, \\qquad\\qquad 2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} = \\dfrac{7\\pi}{4} + 2\\pi n\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x$, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2x =-\\frac{π}{2} + \\frac{π}{4} + 2πn, & 2x =-\\frac{π}{2} + \\frac{7π}{4} + 2πn \\\\ 2x =-\\frac{π}{4} + 2πn, & 2x = \\frac{5π}{4} + 2πn \\\\ x =-\\frac{π}{8} + πn, & x = \\frac{5π}{8} + πn\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100707 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a180dc90-c6b9-577e-9eef-ed60ecafe4e5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Cosine Function"}] :question/id #uuid "ac0a989f-8766-5650-a388-f81206fe76ab" :question/math-academy-id "e-8659" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation:\n$\\cos \\left(6x + 75^\\circ \\right) = -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6x + 75^{∘} &= 135^{∘} + n \\cdot 360^{∘}, \\mid 6x + 75^{∘}|= 225^{∘} + n \\cdot 360^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x$, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}6x &= 60^{∘} + n \\cdot 360^{∘} & 6x|= 150^{∘} + n \\cdot 360^{∘} \\\\ x|= 10^{∘} + n \\cdot 60^{∘} & x|= 25^{∘} + n \\cdot 60^{∘}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101320 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ea83062-5744-52ef-9b3e-f9805ed092fb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f3212f7-2bbb-57b8-989b-fea88f88eb35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "110" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099517} {:answer/id #uuid "09faa734-92ee-567c-b20b-7a2dffc50718" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "240" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099518} {:answer/id #uuid "0a6a0152-99a7-568c-a9a4-bee833e70c76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "160" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099519} {:answer/id #uuid "0b7348e7-7606-5fe7-a1af-d3aea2703612" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "210" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099520} {:answer/id #uuid "570cc21b-9087-50e4-9da7-f38c0f5bb041" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099521}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a6a0152-99a7-568c-a9a4-bee833e70c76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "160" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099519} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ea3b4b7-d26a-533c-8b3c-d836bed86da8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099516}] :question/id #uuid "9d1cd618-3e37-5bc5-a865-78591e0eea79" :question/math-academy-id "q-42788" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$\\sec (\\frac{x}{4} + 20^{∘}) = 2$.\nThe general solution of this equation is\n$x = a^{∘} + 1440^{∘} \\cdot n, x = 1120^{∘} + 1440^{∘} \\cdot n$,\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101321 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ea83062-5744-52ef-9b3e-f9805ed092fb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3ef9952-18b2-58f7-85f8-0f072bfa89eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3π}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099523} {:answer/id #uuid "d67415c6-71ee-5b67-8e0d-760ba6936c08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5π}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099524} {:answer/id #uuid "13b70d9b-a3d1-5d67-8aac-995a284d08b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7π}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099525} {:answer/id #uuid "3b6b0c63-e3e2-5a6d-93d3-daec6e69f03c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099526} {:answer/id #uuid "6b032a6b-ce11-5356-9e27-024c3b6892ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13b70d9b-a3d1-5d67-8aac-995a284d08b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7π}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099525} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6c7da5f-c824-5006-92f3-48ac4254f60a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099522}] :question/id #uuid "bd51b773-7114-5c60-8ae3-bd4c43f5e27a" :question/math-academy-id "q-42789" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$\\csc 2x =-2$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n$x = a + πn, x = \\frac{11π}{12} + πn$,\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a$?"}]}
